TITLE:: RLJust
summary:: Just intonation as a lattice of prime exponents, with its commas and its maps to equal divisions
categories:: Libraries>reLation
related:: Classes/RLPitchSystem, Classes/RLEDO, Classes/RLMorphism, Guides/reLation

DESCRIPTION::
A link::Classes/RLPitchSystem:: whose pitch classes are Arrays of exponents, one for each of the system's odd primes, and whose pitches have the exponent of 2 in front: with code::RLJust([3, 5])::, the pitch class code::[-1, 1]:: is 5/3 and the pitch code::[-1, 1, 0]:: is 3/2.

The lattice is where every equal division comes from: link::#-temperPc:: sends a pitch class to a division's step through its val (link::Classes/RLEDO#-val::), and link::#-kernel:: lists the commas the division tempers out. A closed walk of a division, lifted to the lattice, ends on one of them (link::Classes/RLMorphism#-lift::).

code::
~just = RLJust([3, 5]);
~just.interval([3, 2]);            // [1, 0]: one step along 3
~just.interval([6, 5]);            // [1, -1]: a fifth up, a major third down
~just.name([-1, 1]);               // 5/3
~just.cents([0, -3]);              // 41.06: three major thirds down, the diesis 128/125
~just.commaName([4, -1]);          // syntonic comma 81/80
~just.temperPc(RLEDO(19), [0, 3]); // 18: the diesis is a step of 19
~just.kernel(RLEDO(12), 4);        // [[4, 2], [4, -1], [0, 3], [4, -4] ...]: diaschisma, syntonic comma, diesis, major diesis
RLJust([3, 5, 7]).interval([7, 4]); // [0, 0, 1]
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: primes
The odd primes of the lattice, code::[3, 5]:: by default (the 5-limit).

METHOD:: commas
The table of known commas and small steps, code::[[numerator, denominator], name]:: each.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: primes

METHOD:: rank
The number of primes.

METHOD:: interval
METHOD:: pitchInterval
The exponents of a just ratio, without the exponent of 2 (interval) or with it in front (pitchInterval). A ratio that needs a prime outside the lattice is an Error.

METHOD:: ratioOf
A pitch class as a ratio between 1 and 2, code::[numerator, denominator]:: (Floats: exact up to 2 ** 53).

METHOD:: name
A pitch class as code::"5/3"::; as powers of the primes when the numbers are too large.

METHOD:: commaName
The name of a comma or of a small step, in either direction (code::[4, -1]:: and code::[-4, 1]:: are both the syntonic comma), or nil.

METHOD:: temperPc
METHOD:: temperPitch
A pitch class, or a pitch, in an equal division: the sum of its exponents times the division's steps for each prime.
argument:: edo
An link::Classes/RLEDO::.

METHOD:: kernel
The commas an equal division tempers out: the pitch classes sent to 0 with exponents up to strong::bound::, one of each pair (x, -x), the smallest in cents first.
argument:: edo
argument:: bound
6 by default.
